WEBVTT

00:01.466 --> 00:03.092
KATARA: Water...

00:03.927 --> 00:05.386
Earth...

00:05.720 --> 00:07.305
Fire...

00:07.847 --> 00:09.349
Air.

00:10.225 --> 00:13.770
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:14.354 --> 00:18.483
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:18.775 --> 00:21.361
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:21.444 --> 00:22.695
could stop them.

00:22.779 --> 00:24.531
But when the world
needed him most,

00:24.614 --> 00:25.782
he vanished.

00:26.199 --> 00:27.450
100 years passed,

00:27.534 --> 00:29.994
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

00:30.078 --> 00:31.746
An airbender named Aang.

00:31.829 --> 00:33.957
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:34.040 --> 00:36.626
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:36.709 --> 00:37.794
AANG: Oof.

00:37.961 --> 00:41.005
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:49.597 --> 00:51.224
AZULA: If I want to catch my prey,

00:51.307 --> 00:52.976
I must be agile, nimble.

00:53.059 --> 00:55.019
I need a small elite team.

00:56.938 --> 01:00.567
TOPH: Even though I was born blind,
I've never had a problem seeing.

01:00.650 --> 01:02.569
I see with earthbending.

01:03.236 --> 01:05.446
AANG: You're going to be
a great teacher, Toph.

01:05.863 --> 01:07.782
I thought a lot about
what you said.

01:07.865 --> 01:09.784
You did? Good, good.

01:10.034 --> 01:12.704
We no longer have
anything to gain by traveling together.

01:13.788 --> 01:15.415
I need to find my own way.

01:29.596 --> 01:32.015
Hey, you guys picked
a great campsite.

01:32.473 --> 01:34.267
The grass is so soft.

01:34.475 --> 01:36.853
That's not grass. Appa's shedding.

01:36.936 --> 01:38.146
Oh, gross.

01:38.479 --> 01:39.606
AANG: That's not gross.

01:39.689 --> 01:41.482
It's just a part of spring.

01:41.566 --> 01:43.234
You know, rebirth,
flowers blooming,

01:43.318 --> 01:44.861
and Appa gets a new coat.

01:45.153 --> 01:47.488
Ahh. The beauty of spring.

01:48.781 --> 01:50.241
( GROWLING )

01:51.534 --> 01:52.952
Stop. Appa, stop!

01:53.036 --> 01:55.121
( COUGHING )

01:55.204 --> 01:58.750
It's not that bad, Katara.
It makes a great wig.

01:58.833 --> 02:00.251
And a great beard.

02:00.335 --> 02:01.711
( BOYS LAUGHING )

02:01.794 --> 02:04.714
I'm just glad we finally have
another girl in the group,

02:04.797 --> 02:06.466
because you two are disgusting.

02:07.467 --> 02:09.594
Excuse me.
Does anyone have a razor,

02:09.677 --> 02:12.680
because I got some hairy pits.

02:12.764 --> 02:14.307
( LAUGHTER )

02:14.390 --> 02:15.558
( SNEEZES )

02:18.394 --> 02:19.812
( CHUCKLES )

02:30.198 --> 02:32.533
So, Toph, usually when
setting up camp,

02:32.617 --> 02:34.160
we try to divide up the work.

02:34.744 --> 02:37.872
Hey, don't worry about me. I'm good to go.

02:37.955 --> 02:40.208
Well, actually, what I'm trying to say is

02:40.291 --> 02:42.043
some of us might fetch water

02:42.126 --> 02:44.212
while someone else
might set up the fire pit

02:44.295 --> 02:45.296
or put up the tent.

02:45.630 --> 02:47.340
Even Momo does his fair share.

02:47.715 --> 02:50.635
Katara, I'm fine.
I can carry my own weight.

02:50.718 --> 02:53.429
I don't need a fire.
I've already collected my own food.

02:53.638 --> 02:57.100
And look. My tent's all set up.

02:57.183 --> 03:00.103
Well, that's great for you,
but we still need to finish―

03:00.186 --> 03:02.897
I don't understand.
What's the problem here?

03:02.980 --> 03:04.357
Never mind.

03:09.362 --> 03:10.738
Oops. Sorry.

03:16.869 --> 03:19.664
Hey, Toph, I wanted to apologize
for earlier.

03:19.747 --> 03:21.582
I think we're all just a little tired

03:21.666 --> 03:23.292
and getting on each
other's nerves.

03:23.376 --> 03:25.753
Yeah. You do seem pretty tired.

03:26.504 --> 03:27.880
I meant all of us.

03:28.089 --> 03:30.341
Well, good night.

03:31.175 --> 03:32.468
Good night.

03:43.062 --> 03:44.897
There's something coming toward us.

03:45.189 --> 03:46.482
AANG: What is it?

03:46.566 --> 03:51.070
It feels like an avalanche,
but also not an avalanche.

03:51.571 --> 03:54.031
Your powers of perception
are frightening.

03:54.490 --> 03:55.700
Should we leave?

03:55.783 --> 03:57.034
Better safe than sorry.

04:02.790 --> 04:03.916
What is that thing?

04:08.171 --> 04:09.213
( SNORING )

04:10.006 --> 04:11.132
( YAWNS )

04:19.974 --> 04:22.810
Ah, land, sweet land.

04:23.686 --> 04:25.104
See you guys in the morning.

04:25.188 --> 04:26.856
Actually, can you help us unload?

04:26.939 --> 04:29.400
Really? You need me to help unload

04:29.484 --> 04:31.527
Sokka's funky-smelling sleeping bag?

04:32.028 --> 04:33.029
( SNIFFS )

04:33.112 --> 04:34.363
Well, yeah.

04:35.198 --> 04:36.449
That and everything else.

04:36.532 --> 04:38.201
You're a part of our team now and―

04:38.284 --> 04:40.995
Look, I didn't ask you to unload my stuff.

04:41.078 --> 04:42.580
I'm carrying
my own weight.

04:42.663 --> 04:43.998
That's not the point.

04:44.457 --> 04:45.708
Ever since you joined us,

04:45.792 --> 04:48.211
you've been nothing
but selfish and unhelpful.

04:48.294 --> 04:51.088
What? Look here, sugar queen.

04:51.172 --> 04:52.965
I gave up everything I had

04:53.049 --> 04:55.009
so that I could teach Aang earthbending.

04:55.092 --> 04:58.387
So don't you talk to me
about being selfish.

04:59.972 --> 05:01.265
"Sugar queen"?!

05:02.141 --> 05:05.019
D―did you just slam the door in my face?

05:05.353 --> 05:07.939
How can you be so infuriating?

05:08.356 --> 05:10.483
Should we do something?

05:10.566 --> 05:12.193
Hey, I'm just enjoying the show.

05:12.985 --> 05:15.905
Ok, ok. You both need to calm down.

05:16.155 --> 05:18.157
Both?! I'm completely calm!

05:19.200 --> 05:21.035
I can see that.

05:26.791 --> 05:29.377
The stars sure are
beautiful tonight.

05:29.460 --> 05:31.504
Too bad you can't see them, Toph.

05:31.587 --> 05:32.672
( TOPH GRUNTS )

05:32.755 --> 05:33.881
( KATARA SCREAMS )

05:34.549 --> 05:36.300
Hey, how's a guy supposed to sleep

05:36.384 --> 05:38.594
with all this yelling and earthquaking?

05:39.804 --> 05:40.972
That thing is back.

05:41.472 --> 05:43.182
Well, how far away is it?

05:43.266 --> 05:46.644
Maybe we can close our eyes
just for a few minutes.

05:47.645 --> 05:49.397
AANG: I don't think so, Sokka.

05:55.278 --> 05:57.363
Seriously, what is that thing?

05:57.446 --> 05:59.574
And how does it keep finding us?

06:00.032 --> 06:02.201
I don't know, but this time,

06:02.285 --> 06:04.120
I'm gonna make sure we lose them.

06:19.510 --> 06:21.762
SOKKA: Ok, forget about setting up camp.

06:21.846 --> 06:25.308
I'm finding the softest pile of dirt
and going to sleep.

06:25.808 --> 06:28.394
That's good, because Toph wasn't
going to help anyway.

06:28.477 --> 06:32.273
Oh, I didn't realize baby still needed
someone to tuck her in bed.

06:32.356 --> 06:34.358
Come on, guys. There's something after us,

06:34.442 --> 06:36.777
and we don't even
know what or who it is.

06:37.153 --> 06:40.239
It could be Zuko.
We haven't seen him since the north pole.

06:40.323 --> 06:41.574
Who's Zuko?

06:41.657 --> 06:43.743
Oh, just some angry freak
with a ponytail

06:43.826 --> 06:45.703
who's tracked us all over the world.

06:45.786 --> 06:48.623
What's wrong with ponytails, ponytail?

06:48.706 --> 06:51.876
This is a warrior's wolf tail.

06:51.959 --> 06:54.295
Well, it certainly tells
the other warriors

06:54.378 --> 06:56.130
that you're fun and perky.

06:56.547 --> 06:59.675
Anyway, whoever's chasing us,
they couldn't have followed us here,

06:59.759 --> 07:03.012
so, now, would everyone just shush?

07:03.846 --> 07:05.473
( MOMO CHATTERING )

07:05.556 --> 07:09.852
No, Momo. Shh. Sleepy time.

07:14.482 --> 07:16.192
Oh, don't tell me.

07:16.275 --> 07:19.487
That's impossible.
There's no way they could have tracked us.

07:19.570 --> 07:22.073
I can feel it with my own two feet.

07:28.746 --> 07:29.914
Let's get out of here.

07:29.997 --> 07:32.458
Maybe we should face them
and find out who they are.

07:32.541 --> 07:34.168
Who knows? Maybe they're friendly.

07:34.251 --> 07:35.753
Always the optimist.

07:56.649 --> 07:58.484
( LIZARDS HISSING )

08:01.362 --> 08:03.197
It's those three girls from Omashu.

08:03.739 --> 08:06.492
We can take them― Three on three.

08:06.575 --> 08:08.327
Actually, Toph, there's four of us.

08:08.411 --> 08:10.663
Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't count you.

08:10.746 --> 08:12.164
You know, no bending and all.

08:12.248 --> 08:13.916
I can still fight!

08:14.000 --> 08:16.460
Ok, three on three plus Sokka.

08:16.544 --> 08:17.545
( SOKKA GROWLS )

08:22.925 --> 08:25.761
Well, we wanted to find out who they were,
and we found out.

08:25.845 --> 08:27.138
Now, let's get out of here.

08:40.401 --> 08:41.527
Appa, yip yip!

08:50.286 --> 08:54.081
KATARA: I can't believe those girls
followed us all the way from Omashu.

08:54.165 --> 08:56.667
I still think we
could have taken them.

08:56.751 --> 08:59.378
Are you kidding me?
The crazy blue firebending

08:59.462 --> 09:01.756
and the flying daggers
are bad enough,

09:01.839 --> 09:03.340
but the last time we saw them,

09:03.632 --> 09:06.427
one of those girls
did something that took my bending away.

09:06.510 --> 09:07.511
That's scary.

09:07.803 --> 09:10.347
SOKKA: Oh, no. The sun is rising.

09:10.431 --> 09:12.641
We've been up all night
with no sleep.

09:13.267 --> 09:14.560
Sokka, we'll be ok.

09:15.019 --> 09:16.062
Are you sure?

09:16.145 --> 09:17.646
I've never not slept before.

09:17.730 --> 09:19.982
What if I fall asleep now
and something happens?

09:20.066 --> 09:22.109
And something always happens!

09:22.359 --> 09:24.570
Every time we land,
those girls are there.

09:24.653 --> 09:26.447
So we'll just have
to keep flying.

09:27.114 --> 09:28.908
AANG: We can't keep flying forever.

09:35.247 --> 09:37.208
( CALLING )

09:43.839 --> 09:45.007
( AANG YAWNS )

09:45.758 --> 09:47.176
So what's our plan?

09:47.259 --> 09:48.761
Don't know.

09:48.844 --> 09:50.596
Too tired to think.

09:50.805 --> 09:53.724
I'm sure we'll come up with something
after a short nap.

09:54.558 --> 09:56.769
Yes! Sleep.

10:01.190 --> 10:02.942
What's going on?!

10:03.025 --> 10:04.652
Appa fell asleep.

10:04.735 --> 10:06.070
( KIDS SCREAMING )

10:09.031 --> 10:10.032
Wake up, buddy!

10:10.449 --> 10:12.159
( KIDS SCREAMING )

10:27.174 --> 10:28.968
Appa's exhausted.

10:29.385 --> 10:32.638
Ok, we've put a lot of distance
between us and them.

10:33.097 --> 10:36.642
The plan right now is to follow
Appa's lead and get some sleep.

10:36.725 --> 10:39.103
Of course, we could have
gotten some sleep earlier

10:39.186 --> 10:40.938
if Toph didn't have such issues.

10:41.355 --> 10:42.356
What?!

10:42.690 --> 10:45.401
All right, all right!
Everyone's exhausted.

10:45.484 --> 10:47.194
Let's just get some rest.

10:47.403 --> 10:50.239
No. I want to hear what Katara has to say.

10:50.698 --> 10:52.241
You think I have issues?

10:52.616 --> 10:55.077
I'm just saying,
maybe if you helped out earlier,

10:55.161 --> 10:57.955
we could have set up our camp faster
and gotten some sleep.

10:58.038 --> 11:00.374
And then maybe we wouldn't
be in this situation.

11:00.791 --> 11:02.418
TOPH: You're blaming me for this?

11:04.962 --> 11:07.464
No. No! She's not blaming you.

11:07.548 --> 11:08.632
No, I'm blaming her.

11:08.716 --> 11:09.842
- Hey!
- Uh!

11:09.925 --> 11:11.760
I never asked you for diddly-dooda.

11:11.844 --> 11:13.262
I carry my own weight.

11:13.804 --> 11:17.349
Besides, if there's anyone to blame,
it's Sheddy over here.

11:17.433 --> 11:19.351
AANG: What? You're blaming Appa?

11:19.727 --> 11:22.146
Yeah. You want to know
how they keep finding us?

11:22.229 --> 11:24.648
He's leaving a trail
everywhere we go.

11:25.024 --> 11:28.402
How dare you blame Appa.
He saved your life three times today.

11:28.485 --> 11:30.696
If there's anyone to blame, it's you.

11:31.155 --> 11:33.908
You're always talking
about how you carry your own weight,

11:33.991 --> 11:36.702
But you're not. He is.
Appa's carrying your weight.

11:36.994 --> 11:40.039
He never had a problem
flying when it was just the three of us.

11:41.457 --> 11:42.958
I'm out of here.

11:44.919 --> 11:45.920
Wait.

11:59.433 --> 12:00.893
What did I just do?

12:01.143 --> 12:03.729
I can't believe
I yelled at my earthbending teacher.

12:03.812 --> 12:05.481
Now she's gone.

12:05.564 --> 12:09.360
I know. We're all
just trying to get used to each other.

12:09.443 --> 12:11.070
And I was so mean to her.

12:11.737 --> 12:14.031
Yeah, you two were pretty much jerks.

12:14.114 --> 12:15.908
- Thanks, Sokka.
- No problem.

12:16.408 --> 12:18.619
We need to find
Toph and apologize.

12:18.702 --> 12:20.621
Ok, but what are we gonna do

12:20.704 --> 12:23.123
about the tank full
of dangerous ladies chasing us?

12:25.626 --> 12:26.835
I have a plan.

12:37.221 --> 12:38.222
Ugh.

12:38.681 --> 12:42.226
AANG: Toph was right. Appa's fur
was leading a trail right to us.

12:42.685 --> 12:44.687
But now that he's clean,
no more trail.

12:44.770 --> 12:46.772
KATARA: Are you sure he's ok to fly?

12:47.189 --> 12:50.401
He'll be fine as long as we leave
his saddle and all our stuff here.

12:50.484 --> 12:54.029
I'm gonna use Appa's fur to make
a fake trail and lead the tank off-course.

13:14.967 --> 13:15.968
Uh!

13:17.303 --> 13:18.512
Ohh.

13:19.263 --> 13:22.224
That really hurt my tailbone.

13:27.146 --> 13:29.023
Wads of wet fur.

13:29.398 --> 13:30.566
How delightful.

13:30.941 --> 13:35.863
Hmm, they're not wads.
They're more like bundles.

13:35.946 --> 13:37.823
Or bunches?

13:37.906 --> 13:39.908
It's got an "uh" sound.

13:41.160 --> 13:42.494
Clumps.

13:42.578 --> 13:45.039
Clumps! They're clumps!

13:49.960 --> 13:51.503
The trail goes this way.

13:56.800 --> 13:58.719
The Avatar is trying
to give us the slip.

13:58.802 --> 14:01.972
You two head in that direction
and keep your eye out for the bison.

14:02.598 --> 14:04.350
I'll follow this trail.

15:06.995 --> 15:08.705
Toph couldn't have
made it too far.

15:08.789 --> 15:09.873
( SCREECHES )

15:09.957 --> 15:11.542
What is it, Momo?! Oh, no!

15:12.042 --> 15:13.460
Katara!

15:13.544 --> 15:15.254
How did they find us?

15:16.755 --> 15:19.007
SOKKA: Appa, come on.
We need to go faster.

15:19.091 --> 15:20.717
KATARA: He's too tired.

15:20.801 --> 15:22.261
Not good, not good!

15:24.930 --> 15:26.974
We just need to make it
across that river.

15:28.142 --> 15:29.977
Come on, Appa! Just a little further.

15:35.941 --> 15:36.942
Whoa!

15:43.449 --> 15:45.075
SOKKA: We made it. We're safe.

15:45.159 --> 15:46.660
KATARA: You did it, Appa!

16:28.827 --> 16:30.162
Good try, but no.

16:38.420 --> 16:39.421
How you doing?

16:39.505 --> 16:40.672
Well, you know.

16:41.215 --> 16:43.675
I thought when Ty Lee and I finally
caught you guys,

16:43.759 --> 16:45.594
it would be more exciting.

16:45.677 --> 16:48.138
Oh, well, victory is boring.

16:48.889 --> 16:50.349
- Aah!
- Aah!

16:53.393 --> 16:55.896
Thanks, Appa.
I don't know what we'd do without you.

17:01.276 --> 17:03.862
Was it just me,
or was that guy kind of cute?

17:20.170 --> 17:21.964
All right. You've caught up with me.

17:22.047 --> 17:23.882
Now, who are you,
and what do you want?

17:24.550 --> 17:28.345
You mean, you haven't guessed?
You don't see the family resemblance.

17:28.428 --> 17:29.805
Here's a hint.

17:29.888 --> 17:31.723
( IMITATING ZUKO )
I must find the Avatar

17:31.807 --> 17:33.183
to restore my honor.

17:34.309 --> 17:36.186
( REGULAR VOICE ) It's ok. You can laugh.

17:36.353 --> 17:37.354
It's funny.

17:38.146 --> 17:39.398
So what now?

17:39.481 --> 17:43.986
Now? Now it's over.
You're tired, and you have no place to go.

17:44.236 --> 17:46.029
You can run, but I'll catch you.

17:47.281 --> 17:48.657
I'm not running.

17:58.292 --> 18:00.127
Here is your tea.

18:02.254 --> 18:05.716
You seem a little
too young to be traveling alone.

18:06.800 --> 18:08.343
You seem a little too old.

18:09.094 --> 18:10.554
Ha ha ha!

18:10.637 --> 18:12.264
Perhaps I am.

18:13.307 --> 18:14.766
I know what you're thinking,

18:14.850 --> 18:17.311
I look like I can't handle
being by myself.

18:17.894 --> 18:19.396
I wasn't thinking that.

18:19.855 --> 18:22.524
You wouldn't let me pour
my own cup of tea.

18:23.066 --> 18:26.570
I poured your tea
because I wanted to

18:26.653 --> 18:28.572
and for no other reason.

18:29.072 --> 18:31.199
People see me
and think I'm weak.

18:31.283 --> 18:32.909
They want to take care of me,

18:32.993 --> 18:36.163
but I can take care of myself by myself.

18:36.496 --> 18:38.332
You sound like my nephew,

18:38.790 --> 18:42.294
Always thinking
you need to do things on your own

18:42.377 --> 18:44.796
without anyone's support.

18:45.047 --> 18:49.635
There is nothing wrong
with letting people who love you help you.

18:49.968 --> 18:52.846
Not that I love you.
Well, I just met you.

18:53.180 --> 18:54.431
( CHUCKLES )

18:54.681 --> 18:57.017
So where is your nephew?

18:57.476 --> 18:59.519
I've been tracking him, actually.

18:59.853 --> 19:01.104
Is he lost?

19:02.105 --> 19:03.857
Yes, a little bit.

19:04.358 --> 19:07.110
His life has recently changed,

19:07.194 --> 19:10.280
And he's going through
very difficult times.

19:10.781 --> 19:14.117
He's trying to figure out who he is,

19:14.201 --> 19:15.702
and he went away.

19:16.036 --> 19:17.996
So now you're following him.

19:18.497 --> 19:21.625
I know he doesn't
want me around right now,

19:21.708 --> 19:24.836
but if he needs me, I'll be there.

19:25.128 --> 19:27.381
Your nephew is very lucky,

19:27.464 --> 19:28.757
even if he doesn't know it.

19:30.509 --> 19:31.551
Thank you.

19:31.635 --> 19:35.847
My pleasure. Sharing tea
with a fascinating stranger

19:35.931 --> 19:39.017
is one of life's true delights.

19:39.101 --> 19:41.311
No. Thank you for what you said.

19:41.978 --> 19:44.731
- It helped me.
- I'm glad.

19:45.649 --> 19:48.610
Oh, and about your nephew,

19:48.694 --> 19:51.113
maybe you should tell him
that you need him, too.

19:55.659 --> 19:57.119
( LIZARD HISSING )

19:59.329 --> 20:01.289
Do you really want to fight me?

20:02.958 --> 20:05.627
Yes. I really do.

20:06.002 --> 20:07.003
Zuko!

20:07.087 --> 20:09.131
I was wondering
when you'd show up, Zu-Zu.

20:09.631 --> 20:11.466
Ha ha. Zu-zu?

20:11.883 --> 20:14.511
Back off, Azula. He's mine.

20:15.721 --> 20:17.973
I'm not going anywhere.

21:06.772 --> 21:08.523
( YELLS )

21:19.993 --> 21:21.661
Whoa! Aah!

21:42.974 --> 21:44.601
Aah!

21:58.782 --> 21:59.908
Katara!

22:10.919 --> 22:12.170
Uncle.

22:12.254 --> 22:13.672
Get up.

22:24.307 --> 22:26.351
I thought you guys
could use a little help.

22:26.726 --> 22:27.811
Thanks.

22:36.778 --> 22:38.697
Well, look at this.

22:38.780 --> 22:41.867
Enemies and traitors all working together.

22:42.742 --> 22:45.203
I'm done.
I know when I'm beaten.

22:45.537 --> 22:49.249
You got me.
A princess surrenders with honor.

22:56.548 --> 22:57.716
Aah!

22:58.675 --> 22:59.676
( YELLS )

23:15.901 --> 23:17.193
Get away from us!

23:22.574 --> 23:23.992
Zuko, I can help.

23:24.743 --> 23:26.328
Leave!
